{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"I removed a stuck finalizer from a ConfigMap and submitted the mitigation. The submission endpoint returned 200. I couldn't confirm that the stuck ConfigMap was what degraded service for users.\n\n- **Finding:** The ConfigMap `reservation-cleanup-token` was stuck in `Terminating` because of the finalizer `cleanup.reservations.io/pending-cleanup`. The `cleanup-controller` is supposed to remove that finalizer. It was looping on HTTP 403 errors because its ClusterRole `configmap-cleanup-controller` only allows get, list and watch on ConfigMaps, not patch.\n- **Fix:** I cleared the finalizer by hand with `kubectl patch`, and the ConfigMap is now gone.\n- **Check:** All pods were Running with healthy logs. A test request to `frontend:5000/hotels` returned 200 in about 7 ms.\n- **Not fixed:** I did not change the ClusterRole. The controller will hit the same 403 on any future stuck ConfigMap until it is granted `patch` on ConfigMaps."}}
